{% block body %}
<div class="container">
{% set position = {
    id: 2,
    company: "Qonys inc",
    name: "Data Scientist",
    description: "# Job Description: Junior Data Scientist

**Company:** Qonys  
**Position Title:** Data Scientist  
**Level:** Junior  
**Location:** Remote / Hybrid  
**Department:** Analytics & AI Solutions  
**Employment Type:** Full-time  

---

## 📋 Role Overview

At **Qonys**, we build data-driven products that empower decision-making across complex industries. We are looking for a motivated and detail-oriented **Junior Data Scientist** to join our growing analytics team. 

In this role, you will collaborate closely with senior data engineers, machine learning specialists, and product managers to process data, build predictive models, and deliver key analytical insights.

---

## 🎯 Key Responsibilities

- **Data Processing & Analysis:** Extract, clean, and analyze datasets to identify trends, patterns, and operational insights.
- **Model Development:** Support the design, training, and deployment of predictive and statistical models using Python and modern data science stacks.
- **Feature Engineering:** Build meaningful features from structured and unstructured data sources to improve model accuracy.
- **Dashboarding & Visualization:** Construct interactive reports and dashboards to convey analytical insights to non-technical stakeholders.
- **Cross-functional Collaboration:** Work alongside software developers to integrate machine learning solutions into live product workflows.
- **Code Optimization & Testing:** Write clean, modular, and reusable code while maintaining standard version control practices (Git).

---

## 🛠 Required Qualifications & Skills

### Technical Skills
- **Language Proficiency:** Strong command of **Python** (Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, Matplotlib/Seaborn).
- **Database & Querying:** Solid understanding of **SQL** for data extraction, joining, and aggregation.
- **Mathematics & Statistics:** Strong foundational knowledge in probability, linear algebra, and hypothesis testing.
- **Language Requirements:** Fluency in English with a target score equivalent to **IELTS 6.5+** or higher.

### Soft Skills & Candidate Attributes
- **Problem Solving:** Analytical mindset with a structured approach to troubleshooting data issues.
- **Communication:** Ability to clearly explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences.
- **Adaptability:** Eagerness to learn new libraries, frameworks, and domain-specific knowledge rapidly.

---

## 🌟 Preferred / Bonus Qualifications

- Experience with Big Data frameworks (e.g., PySpark, SQL-based data warehouses).
- Basic understanding of cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, or Azure).
- Familiarity with version control systems (Git/GitHub) and containerization (Docker).
- Exposure to NLP or deep learning frameworks (PyTorch or TensorFlow).

---

## 💼 What We Offer

- **Competitive Compensation:** Market-aligned salary with annual performance reviews.
- **Professional Growth:** Dedicated learning budget for courses, certifications, and conferences.
- **Flexible Work Environment:** Hybrid working arrangement with flexible core hours.
- **Comprehensive Benefits:** Health coverage, paid time off (PTO), and wellness stipends.

---

